      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm setting up some new data processes for my stationery shop in lyon to be gdpr compliant. i'm mostly focused on the obvious stuff like customer names and emails, but i'm also a bit worried about the less obvious, \"unseen\" data—like small bits of info left in system logs or background files that might be floating around without me realizing it. what are the rules for how i should handle these kinds of hidden or secondary data fragments to make sure there aren't any sneaky risks?",
